WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:05.700
Speaker 1: One of the most anticipated debates
in the 2022 election cycle was last night.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:12.849
It was quack television, Dr. Mehmet Oz against
Democratic Pennsylvania Lieutenant Governor

00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:14.009
John Fetterman.

00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:17.900
They are vying to be the next senator from
Pennsylvania.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.180
Now, I am not going to sugarcoat this for
anybody.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.270
And I didn't during yesterday's much watched
live stream.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:28.660
John Fetterman suffered a stroke some months
ago.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:34.850
He is recovering and has been cleared by his
doctors to say you can serve as senator.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:41.980
He is not struggling cognitively in the sense
of memory, logic, critical thinking.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:49.550
But Fetterman is struggling significantly
when it comes to speaking and translating

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.910
thought into speech.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.850
It's really sad to see.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:01:02.280
And what is horrifying is that the completely
unqualified, delusional and incompetent Mehmet

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.159
Oz.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:09.060
May become a senator because John Fetterman
had a stroke.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.850
And didn't perform particularly well last
night.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.689
It was difficult to watch.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:17.020
I'm putting politics aside here for a second.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.950
I feel terribly for John Fetterman.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:24.920
A public figure in the middle of a campaign
has a stroke running for an important office

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.439
and now visibly struggles to speak.

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:36.049
Needed closed captioning during yesterday's
debate in order to better understand the subject

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:41.299
matter having having trouble with order to
auditory processing.

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:45.149
I hope for the absolute best for letterman's
recovery.

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:48.240
And it was a very difficult debate to watch
last night.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.490
By the way, Fetterman was not a particularly
good debater.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:54.729
I mean, Fetterman was the best candidate in
the Democratic primary.

00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:59.100
But even at the Democratic primary debates,
he wasn't the best debater.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.200
Let's look at a few clips from last night.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.750
The most disturbing clip was when Mehmet Oz
said that local political leaders should be

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:11.090
the ones making decisions, along with patients
and doctors about abortion.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.430
No, they shouldn't.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:14.630
It should be doctors and patients.

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:17.950
But here is Oz with a very extreme statement.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:22.220
Speaker 2: There should not be involvement
from the federal government in how states

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.370
decide their abortion decisions.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:28.739
As a physician, I've been in the room when
there's some difficult conversations happening.

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:31.470
I don't want the federal government involved
with that at all.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:36.790
I want women, doctors, local political leaders
letting the democracy that always allowed

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:39.030
our nation to thrive, to put the best ideas
forward.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:43.010
Speaker 1: So why do we need politicians in
the room?

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.670
Why is it better if they're local?

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:51.739
This idea of let the states decide when there
really aren't differences.

00:02:51.739 --> 00:02:53.200
Let me give you an example.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:59.879
When it comes to gun safety, as an example,
Bernie Sanders is correct that gun ownership

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:07.739
in Vermont is a very different thing socio
culturally than it is in, I don't know, North

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:08.849
Carolina.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:10.810
And so.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:16.510
Regardless of your views, I can understand
why one would say, Well, because gun ownership

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:19.640
in Vermont is a different thing than in North
Carolina.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.310
Maybe there should be a different conversation
happening in each state.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:26.870
It doesn't mean we don't have gun safety regulations
or that I think we shouldn't have them.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:28.980
But it's at least plausible.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:33.690
When it comes to abortion, it's fundamentally
about this is a medical procedure and this

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.799
is a procedure in which you shouldn't have
politicians in the middle.

00:03:37.799 --> 00:03:45.220
Why is it better to have a local, you know,
a governor or a mayor?

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.180
Telling women what they can't do rather than
a senator in DC.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:52.540
Either way, it's bad and this is a completely
outrageous and extreme position.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.540
Here is just a clip.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:57.390
Just to really sum up the difference in the
positions between Mehmet Oz and John Fetterman

00:03:57.390 --> 00:03:58.390
on this issue.

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:03.260
Speaker 2: All I want women, doctors, local
political leaders letting the democracy that

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.319
always allowed our nation to thrive, to put
the best ideas forward so states can decide

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:08.489
for themselves.

00:04:08.489 --> 00:04:10.840
Contrast that with my opponent, John Fetterman.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:16.199
But if you believe that the choice for abortion
belongs between you and your doctor, that's

00:04:16.199 --> 00:04:17.290
what I fight for.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.290
Speaker 1: It's that.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.290
That's.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.290
It's that simple.

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:21.290
It's that simple.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:27.160
And Oz's position, of course, has been cobbled
together in trying to basically focus group

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:32.050
the best possible thing to say exceptions,
but not this and no federal involvement.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:33.610
But let local verb.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.199
It's a mess and it's outrageous and it's extreme.

00:04:36.199 --> 00:04:38.810
The Fetterman position is the correct position.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:44.330
Now, John Fetterman did comment on his stroke,
and he had the following to say about it.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:49.880
Speaker 2: Sylvania Here's a man that spent
more than $20 million of his own money to

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:52.840
try to buy that seat.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:05:00.240
I'm also having the talk about something called
the Oz Rule that if he's on TV, he's lying.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.180
He did that during his career on his TV show.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:09.789
He's done that during his campaign about lying
about our record here.

00:05:09.789 --> 00:05:13.590
And he's also lying probably during this debate.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:16.080
And let's also talk about the elephant in
the room.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.020
I had a stroke.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.789
He's never let me forget that.

00:05:19.789 --> 00:05:23.860
And I might miss some words during this debate.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:24.860
Two words together.

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:25.860
But it knocked me down.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:28.220
But I'm going to keep coming back up.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:33.550
And this campaign is all that to me is about
fighting for every one in Pennsylvania that

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:38.449
ever got knocked down that needs to get back
up and fighting for all forgotten communities

00:05:38.449 --> 00:05:41.060
all across Pennsylvania that also got knocked
down.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.550
That needs to keep solving.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:43.920
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.130
So as you can see.

00:05:48.130 --> 00:05:53.800
It takes a lot of courage to do what Fetterman
did last night.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:06:00.470
It's he's in the middle of a recovery from
a stroke, and he brought it up and it was

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:04.520
really something to see and also quite difficult
to watch.

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:11.699
The issue of the quack cures promoted by Mehmet
Oz on his program came up yesterday and listen

00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:17.770
very carefully to the exact language that
Oz uses, and you will very quickly see why

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.139
he's choosing such narrow language.

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:24.479
Mr. Oz, you have built a lucrative career
around medicine.

00:06:24.479 --> 00:06:29.690
Speaker 2: But you've been criticized even
by some fellow physicians for promoting, quote,

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:34.400
unproven, ill advised and at times potentially
dangerous treatments.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.150
What is your response to that?

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:42.550
You have 60 seconds and what did you or your
company make a profit from promoting those

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:43.550
products?

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:47.540
I never sold weight loss products as as described
in those commercials.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.910
It's like it's a television show.

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:52.770
Like this is a television show so people can
run commercials on the shows.

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:56.210
And that's a perfectly appropriate and very
transparent process.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:57.250
Mm hmm.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:01.070
Speaker 1: I consider the language there.

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:12.160
I never sold weight loss products as described
in John Fetterman commercials.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.860
Okay.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:17.030
That is extraordinarily narrow language.

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:21.940
He provided a platform for those products.

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:24.479
It made the show profitable.

00:07:24.479 --> 00:07:31.030
He was promoting green coffee extract as a
magical weight loss cure that is not evidence

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:32.030
based.

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:38.080
He was promoting raspberry ketones as the,
quote, number one miracle in a bottle to burn

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.539
your fat.

00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:41.110
That is not evidence based.

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:45.289
He promoted guests who say homoeopathy works
uncritically.

00:07:45.289 --> 00:07:48.460
And I know some people in my audience get
mad about this.

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.460
It doesn't work.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:50.780
Guys, I'm sorry.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.389
I know people e-mail me every time.

00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:56.789
There are no active ingredients in homeopathy.

00:07:56.789 --> 00:07:58.690
There are no measurable, active ingredients.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.970
It does not work.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:01.259
It has been widely studied.

00:08:01.259 --> 00:08:02.500
Oh, but David.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.460
Big Pharma won't allow studies, guys.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.539
Homeopathy has been widely studied.

00:08:09.539 --> 00:08:12.430
It doesn't work and Oz promoted it.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:15.520
So extraordinarily narrow language there.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:20.150
Oz also promoting medication supposedly for
colds.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:22.870
The way to get rid of a cold is to wait 5
to 7 days.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:23.870
Okay.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.270
No matter what you take during those 5 to
7 days.

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:27.270
Right.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.789
Coffee enema, which is dangerous, by the way.

00:08:30.789 --> 00:08:38.630
You know, fried plantains, um, baths with
whatever, you know, coconut oil.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:42.289
About 5 to 7 days later, the cold will be
gone.

00:08:42.289 --> 00:08:46.610
And to attribute it to all of these different
supposed cold cures doesn't actually make

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:47.640
any sense.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:51.170
So bottom line, the question with this race
is what happens with the polling?

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:53.310
What happens with the polling at this point
in time?

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:57.140
Because going into yesterday's debate, the
polling is what it is right now.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:59.630
Fetterman Plus 1.3.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.040
Fetterman Plus 1.3.

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:05.160
And if you take a look, you will see that
Fetterman had a nearly nine point lead in

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:09.160
early August, and that lead was only six at
the beginning of September, and that lead

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:14.010
was only four towards the end of September,
and that lead is now 1.3.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:19.760
How much of an impact can a single debate
have on a race like this, particularly when

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:24.440
one candidate is visibly struggling with his
speech as a result of the stroke that he had?

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:28.959
I don't have the answer, but we'll find out
in the next 7 to 10 days, and then the election's

00:09:28.959 --> 00:10:36.329
only two weeks away and then we'll know 

00:10:36.329 --> 00:10:52.899
a lot more.

